Fillets: a face's outline rounded past a cylinder's rims rounded with less
than the radius, and past a wall's corner tighter than the ball where the
other wall's edge with the face is obtuse (mitcad#1426).

The case: a tube (bore 25, outside 30, 30 long) cut by a plane U; its rims
rounded with rk = 1 (tori); the outline of each cut face rounded with
R = 1.5, one tangent chain over U's lines on the end planes, the outside
and the bore, and its arcs on the rims' tori. No ball of R rolls round a
rim of rk: OCCT walked the chain over the torus and threw while storing
the walk (the rational sections' weights), on the replayed and on the
stored body. Patch 0970 split such a chain only at a cylinder K between
two planes, and only where the other wall's edge with U is square or
acute. The bodies stored in the files close the bore's rims (whose edge
with U is acute) with 0970's vertex blend and torus, the bore in the
place of the leaning plane, and the outside's rims (obtuse) with the
rim's own ball: the ball of R touching U, the end plane and the outside
lies clear of the rim's torus; the ball of rk that the torus is rolls on
between the outside and the end plane's rounding (a strip), then between
the two roundings (a triangle) down to where their contacts on U meet, as
patch 1380 closes a concave corner.

- ChFi3d_TightArc (0970's) also takes K a torus between the plane Wp
  square to the other line and a cylinder Wo about K's axis whose line on
  U runs along it (K the rim of Wo's edge with Wp: its tube circle rk
  inside both), and marks the corner Obtuse where the other wall's
  outward normal at its line on U turns towards U's (a plane or the
  cylinder Wo); such corners are split too (before, an obtuse wall was
  left as it was).
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformTightCorners: where Wo is such a cylinder, the
  ball's centre C is R inside U, Wp and Wo (on the line R inside U and
  rw -+ R from Wo's axis, on its line's side), e0 Wo's outward normal
  along Lo, K's tube circle through T's spine circle's start, a torus K's
  seams (circles) kept by their direction at the point, K cut along its
  meridian; an obtuse corner goes to PerformTightObtuseCorner.
- ChFi3d_Builder::ExtendAtTightObtuseCorners (new, after
  ExtendAtTightConcaveArcs): the ends at an obtuse corner walk on past
  their vertex by two radii, so that the end plane's rounding's contact
  on it reaches the rim (the strip starts from the rim's section there).
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformSetOfKPart: an end of status ChFiDS_Tangent
  prolonged past its vertex is not cut by the face at the end
  (ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd and the like marked it a free boundary): its
  corner's construction cuts it.
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformTightObtuseCorner (new): 1380's corner
  (tcBuildCorner) with the balls inside the material (Side -1), the
  heights along U's inward normal, K's edges any curves (a torus's seams:
  where a contact reaches them, the strip's first section's contact on
  K's edge with the outside, which side of them is kept).

On the design's stored body before the item: valid, the file's 73 faces,
the result within 0.0057 mm of the stored body about the outlines both
ways, the material taken 83.349390 against the file's 83.349888 mm3;
before, the fillet failed. On the replay's bodies of both designs: the
item parametric and verified. Synthetic: the tube of the case, valid, the
four tori of the file, every point of the strips and triangles on the
rim's ball within 5e-4 mm; a block's bottom outline past vertical corners
rounded with 0.3, its front wall leaning 15 and 30 degrees away from the
bottom, rounded with 0.5: valid (before, invalid at 15 and failed at 30).

